lesson: 113
title: Ages: years ago, years from now
stars: 0
explain: Everyone gets one year older each year, so in 5 years a child of 8 will be 8 + 5 = 13, and 3 years ago was 8 - 3 = 5.
explain: The difference between two ages never changes: if Ben is 4 years older than Mia now, he is 4 years older in every year.
explain: If two ages add up to 20 and one child is 4 years older, take the 4 away and halve: (20 - 4) / 2 = 8 and 8 + 4 = 12.
vars: a=name b=name x=4..12 d=2..9 n=2..10 g=2..6
need: x + d > g + 1
answer: x + d + n
exercise: {a} is {x} years old. {b} is {d} years older than {a}. How old will {b} be in {n} years?
exercise: {b} is {x+d} years old now. How old will {b.he} be in {n} years?
exercise: {g} years ago {b} was {x+d-g} years old. How old will {b} be {n} years from now?
exercise: {b} is {d} years older than {a}. In {n} years {a} will be {x+n}. How old will {b} be then?
exercise: The ages of {a} and {b} add up to {2*x+d}. {b} is {d} years older than {a}. How old will {b} be in {n} years?
exercise: {a} is {x} and {b} is {x+d}. How old will {b} be in {n} years?
test: {b} was {x+d-g} years old {g} years ago. What age will {b.he} be in {n} years' time?
test: In {n} years, how old is {b}, who is {d} years older than {a}, if {a} is {x} today?
test: Together {a} and {b} are {2*x+d} years old, and {b} is the older by {d} years. What will {b}'s age be after {n} more years?
test: {a} will be {x+n} in {n} years. {b} is always {d} years older. How old will {b} be at that time?
exercise: {b} is {x+d} today. What age will {b.he} be in {n} years?
exercise: {a} from Ohio is {x}, and {b} is {d} years older. How old will {b} be in {n} years' time?
exercise: How old will {b} be in {n} years if {b} is {d} years older than {a}, who is {x} now?
exercise: {g} years ago {b} was {x+d-g}. What age will {b} be {n} years from today?
exercise: {a} is {x.words} years old and {b} is {d.words} years older. How old will {b} be after {n.words} years?
exercise: The sum of the ages of {a} and {b} is {2*x+d}, and {b} is {d} years older. How old will {b} be in {n} years?
exercise: In {n} years {a} will be {x+n}. {b} is {d} years older than {a}. What will {b}'s age be then?
exercise: {b} lives in Cork and turned {x+d} this year. How old will {b.he} be in {n} years?
test: {b}, from Sydney, was {x+d-g} years old {g} years back. How old will {b.he} be {n} years from now?
test: {a} and {b} have ages that total {2*x+d}. The difference between their ages is {d}, and {b} is the older. What age will {b} reach in {n} years?
test: {n} years from now, what will be the age of {b}, if {a} is {x} and {b} is {d} years older than {a}?
test: {a} in Vermont is {x} years old. {b} is {d} years older. How old is {b} going to be in {n} years?
test: In {n} years {a} will be {x+n}, and {b} will still be {d} years older. What will {b}'s age be?
test: Today {b} is {x+d}. Add {n} years. How old is {b} then?
exercise: {a}'s {x}, {b}'s {d} years older. how old {b} gonna be in {n} years
exercise: {b} is {x+d+1} — no wait, {x+d} now. how old in {n} years
exercise: {g} years ago {b} was {x+d-g}. {a} says in {n} years {b.he}'ll be {x+d-g+n}. nah, what's the real age
exercise: {a} is {x}, {b} {d} years older, and their dog's 3 lol. {b}'s age in {n} years?
test: how old's {b} gonna be {n} years from now? {b}'s {x+d} today
