exam: It is given that {a} is {x} years of age and that {b} is {d} years older than {a}. Determine the age of {b} {n} years hence.
exam: Ascertain the age which {b}, being presently {x+d} years of age, shall attain upon the expiry of {n.words} years.
exam: Whereas {g} years ago {b} was {x+d-g} years of age, state the age of {b} {n} years from the present date.
exam: Compute the age of {b} in {n} years, given that the ages of {a} and {b} sum to {2*x+d} and that {b} is the elder by {d} years.
exercise: {a} is {x} years old. {a.His} cousin {b} is {d} years older. {b}'s grandad passed away last year at a ripe old age. How old will {b} be in {n} years?
exercise: {b} was economical with the truth and said {b.he} was {x}. Really {b.he} is {d} years older than that. How old will {b} really be in {n} years?
test: {b}'s telling porkies again, says {b.he}'s {x}. crap, {b.he}'s {d} years older than that. how old in {n} years, for real
